> **FICTIONAL DEMONSTRATION DOCUMENT** — International Cheese Federation (ICF), a fictitious trade association created for the MemberJunction More Cheese demonstration environment. All names, figures, events, and decisions are invented.

Agreed, and honestly it improves the post. Friday''s piece now says "members who plan a year at a
time" and links to the membership page instead of quoting a count. The argument was never really
about how many of us there are.

Decision, for the record: **no membership figures in public content until the Individual-tier
variance is closed and we have a defensible new-versus-renewing basis.** I''ll hold that line for
the rest of Q1 and revisit with you in April rather than chase it weekly.

Copying the Office in so this isn''t a surprise if it comes up. Two things I''d like on someone''s
list: the $145 rate, and a plain-English description of what our member count actually counts,
which I will happily write once you tell me what it is.

Post ships tomorrow morning. Thanks for the flag — this was the right catch.

*Communications*'
