This article discusses the complex and often conflicting state and federal regulations impacting farmstead dairies and artisan cheesemakers, particularly concerning raw milk and raw-milk cheeses. It highlights the challenges of direct-to-consumer sales within state borders versus the strict 60-day aging requirement for interstate commerce, and outlines the International Cheese Federation''s advocacy for risk-based regulatory frameworks.
 
