This blog post from the International Cheese Federation discusses the lack of clear federal standards for descriptive terms like ''aged'' and ''farmstead'' on cheese labels, contrasting them with defined standards of identity for cheese types. It highlights the market flattening, legal challenges, and complexities arising from varying state regulations, and announces that the Standards Committee is gathering member input to develop collective solutions for more precise and equitable labeling.
 
