This article features Gwen Whitfield, an International Cheese Federation member and principal at Whitfield Food Safety Training. It details her transition from hands-on cheesemaking to teaching food safety, emphasizing the critical role of accurate record-keeping for inspections, the effectiveness of practical, behavior-focused training, and the evolution of food safety standards from reputation to documentation. Whitfield also notes the increasing engagement of members in food safety sessions.
 
