This article from the International Cheese Federation (ICF) emphasizes the critical importance for specialty cheese producers to track their specific financial metrics, such as milk cost per unit, yield by style, and realized price, rather than relying solely on broader market benchmarks. It advocates for establishing a consistent habit of internal financial tracking to proactively identify and address potential issues. The piece promotes the ''Pricing & Margin for Specialty Cheese'' course, designed to help small producers develop these essential financial management skills.
 
