This blog post from the International Cheese Federation (ICF) announces the first half of its 2019 event calendar. It details two in-person workshops in February: one on cedar packaging in Argentina focusing on breathability and labeling, and another on practical food safety in Pennsylvania covering environmental monitoring and record-keeping. The post also outlines upcoming webinars on judging standards, wholesale negotiation, apprenticeship programs, and rennet alternatives. Additionally, it previews two more workshops in late spring (Meadow Affinage and Curd Retailing) and highlights the ICF Annual Conference in Madison, Wisconsin, in July, including details about the annual cheese competition and advice for international travelers and judges.
 
