This article from the International Cheese Federation (ICF) discusses the current tight cheese market, characterized by high block cheese prices and significantly lower national cheese stocks compared to the previous year. It attributes this tightness to strong demand, particularly from exports, which have outpaced a healthy production pace. The article highlights the resolution of a retaliatory tariff dispute, which has reopened a key export lane to a large southern market, leading to increased orders. It advises members, especially exporters, to re-evaluate their pricing and buyer relationships and ensure their documentation is current, given the volatile market and renewed export opportunities. The ICF plans to monitor domestic stock levels and export recovery and is considering a members-only webinar on trade.
 
