> **FICTIONAL DEMONSTRATION DOCUMENT** — International Cheese Federation (ICF), a fictitious trade association created for the MemberJunction More Cheese demonstration environment. All names, figures, events, and decisions are invented.

## February workshop readiness

- Events Team weekly stand-up
- 5 February 2019
- Two workshops, thirteen and twenty-two days out

> notes: Ten minutes, not thirty. The decision we need today is whether Lancaster gets a push.
> FICTIONAL DEMONSTRATION DOCUMENT — International Cheese Federation, a fictitious trade association created for the MemberJunction More Cheese demonstration environment.

---

## What is in front of us

- Cedar Packaging Workshop — Tandil, 18 February
- Prairie Food Safety Workshop — Lancaster, 27 February
- Both in-person, both $150 registration
- No other ICF event until the spring calendar

> notes: These are the only two events on the books this month. Nothing else competes for attention.

---

## Registration as of 4 February

- Tandil: 25 registered, 13 days out
- Lancaster: 18 registered, 22 days out
- 23 workshop registrations taken last week across both
- Curve is moving; neither is where we want it

> notes: Numbers from the registration table as of Monday. They will be stale by Thursday.

---

## Tandil — Cedar Packaging

- Packaging and cut-and-wrap for small producers
- Strongest topic pull we have in the region
- 13 days out with 25 in the room
- Risk: travel distance for members outside the province

> notes: The topic sells itself. Distance is the only real constraint here.

---

## Lancaster — Prairie Food Safety

- Food safety fundamentals, in-person format
- 22 days out with 18 registered
- Slower start than Tandil despite more runway
- Food Safety Committee has offered to promote it

> notes: This is the one that needs a decision. More runway, fewer registrations.

---

## What we think is happening

- Food safety reads as obligation, not opportunity
- Members book it late, close to the date
- Same pattern showed on last year''s safety sessions
- Not yet a problem; would be one at fifteen days out

> notes: Do not panic-discount. Late booking on compliance topics is normal.

---

## Proposal

- Hold price at $150 — no discount, no bundling
- One targeted reminder to the Lancaster region on 11 February
- Ask Food Safety Committee for one member quote we can use
- Re-check both counts on 12 February and escalate if Lancaster is under 30

> notes: The 12 February checkpoint is the actual ask. Everything else is cheap.

---

## Decisions we need

- Approve the 11 February reminder to the Lancaster list
- Confirm no discount on either workshop
- Name an owner for the 12 February re-check

> notes: If we get these three today the rest runs itself.'
