This article highlights an International Cheese Federation (ICF) member, a small farmstead operator, who consistently engages in advocacy by participating in comment periods, signing petitions, and writing letters on policy issues like interstate shipment rules and raw-milk aging standards. It emphasizes the significant impact of this ''low-visibility work'' from individual producers on legislative staff and encourages other members to contribute their specific experiences to influence policy.
 
