This blog post from the International Cheese Federation discusses the significant impact of a federal government shutdown on the availability of crucial market data, particularly affecting milk pricing and production planning for cheese producers. It highlights the challenges members faced in making sourcing and inventory decisions without timely reports. The article encourages small-batch and farmstead producers to maintain independent cost logs and notes the continued growth of the specialty cheese sector despite data disruptions. Additionally, it addresses member inquiries regarding the federal 60-day aging requirement for raw-milk cheese intended for interstate sale, advising on proper documentation.
 
