This article from the International Cheese Federation clarifies the "qualified facility" exemption under federal preventive-controls rules for small creameries. It emphasizes that while the exemption waives some formal hazard analysis requirements, it still mandates specific documentation, including proof of sales attestation, current labeling, and basic sanitation records. The Federation advises members to regularly review their eligibility to ensure compliance and avoid issues with inspectors.
 
