This member spotlight features a food safety consultant who advises small creameries on developing and implementing effective food safety plans. She highlights the importance of tailoring plans to actual operations rather than relying on generic templates, identifies common pitfalls like misrepresenting practices, and discusses the complexities of raw milk production. The consultant also shares insights from her five years in the field, emphasizing the value of observing real processes, and explains her motivation for joining the International Cheese Federation to stay informed about industry challenges.
 
