This article from the International Cheese Federation discusses how prolonged summer heat and humidity negatively impact dairy milk yield and component quality (butterfat and protein), affecting both farmer income and cheesemaking processes. It offers practical advice for herd managers on monitoring animal health and barn conditions, and for make-room operators on adjusting cheesemaking techniques like curd setting and affinage. The piece also highlights the ''Milk Quality & Herd Health'' course and federal margin-coverage programs as resources for members.
 
