This article from the International Cheese Federation (ICF) clarifies the scope and purpose of the Certified Cheesemonger credential. It details what the exam tests, focusing on practical knowledge like cheese families, production methods, proper storage and handling, food safety, sales, and pairing, rather than just tasting ability. The post also identifies the target audience (retail/wholesale professionals, newer cheesemakers, wholesale reps), suggests study methods, and recommends prerequisite courses like ''Sensory Foundations'' and ''Building a Cheese Counter'', positioning it as a foundational step below the Certified Cheese Professional (CCP) credential.
 
