This article from the International Cheese Federation addresses a record surplus of American, cheddar, and Swiss cheese in cold storage, attributing it to decreased export volumes due to shifting tariff lines and evolving domestic consumer preferences towards natural and imported styles. The surplus is impacting wholesale and raw milk prices. The Federation frames this as an advocacy issue, pushing for solutions like distributing surplus cheese to food-insecure households and improving export access by leveraging member voices against tariff disputes. Members are advised to review contracts and participate in advocacy efforts.
 
