This blog post from the International Cheese Federation discusses two key webinars. The first, ''Judging Standards 2019,'' focused on how competition judges score cheese entries against specific standards, rather than comparative judging, and addressed handling storage/shipping defects. The second, ''Rennet Alternatives 2019,'' scheduled for December, will explore microbial coagulants and fermentation-produced chymosin, aiming to inform members about their impact on cheesemaking processes like yield, affinage, and flavor.
 
