This article from the International Cheese Federation discusses the dual reality of strong, consistent growth in cheese exports, particularly to Mexico and South Korea, juxtaposed with the uncertainty caused by broader trade talk breakdowns and tariff disputes. While current tariffs don''t directly target cheese, the general trade environment indirectly affects buyer and distributor behavior, impacting cheese orders. The piece highlights the opportunities for wholesale producers with export capacity but also points out challenges related to capacity, lead times, paperwork, and payment terms for smaller creameries. It encourages members to leverage ICF resources and connect with experienced exporters for guidance.
 
