This blog post details the annual visit of a French Jura affineur to the International Cheese Federation, highlighting the unique challenges and benefits of his concentrated engagement. It explores the differences in cheesemaking traditions, the impact of trade uncertainties like tariffs on international business, and the value of his perspective on active aging processes for domestic members, despite geographical and time constraints.
 
