This article from the International Cheese Federation discusses the recent improvement in milk prices (Class III and Class IV) and wholesale cheese pricing, offering a much-needed positive margin for producers after two lean years. However, it warns members to prepare for potential future challenges, specifically an ongoing international trade dispute that could lead to new tariffs on imported European cheese. The article advises businesses to review supply contracts, consider contingency plans for imported cheese, and get familiar with the new farm bill''s dairy safety net program.
 
