This article from the International Cheese Federation discusses the challenges affineurs face in managing cheese aging caves during seasonal transitions, particularly in the fall. It highlights how fluctuating outdoor air conditions can lead to uneven humidity and rind development, often masked by summer''s stability. The piece advises on checking airflow patterns beyond sensor readings, analyzing historical data for seasonal shifts, and implementing cost-effective fixes before resorting to expensive equipment replacements. It also promotes relevant courses and member support for managing these environmental controls in cheese maturation.
 
