This article from the International Cheese Federation discusses the ongoing trend of a shrinking national dairy herd and its direct impact on firming milk prices. It advises members, particularly those in the cheese industry, to proactively review their supply contracts and business plans, emphasizing that the long-term trend in herd size is a more reliable indicator than short-term price fluctuations. It also points to a ''Wholesale Negotiation webinar'' as a resource.
 
