This article discusses the federal income-over-feed-cost margin, which triggered safety-net payments for dairy producers for three consecutive months (January, February, March 2019). It highlights that this consistent pattern signals a sustained tightness between feed costs and milk prices. The article explains changes under the new Dairy Margin Coverage program, its retroactive coverage, and incentives for early enrollment. It also encourages producers, especially those not yet enrolled, to use decision tools and consider the program''s benefits, offering assistance through the Membership & Outreach Committee.
 
