This article from the International Cheese Federation discusses the immediate impact of shifting international trade policies, specifically the removal of Mexican tariffs on U.S. cheese and the imposition of new Chinese tariffs on dairy products. It advises both export-active and domestic wholesale members on navigating these changes, emphasizing the importance of understanding tariff effective dates, customs documentation, and how global trade shifts influence domestic supply and pricing negotiations. The federation aims to help members interpret the calendar of trade changes rather than advocate for specific policy outcomes.
 
