This blog post from the International Cheese Federation discusses the implications of a modest spring milk flush on the cheese industry. It highlights how a gentler increase in milk supply, as observed this year, is beneficial for maintaining consistent cheese quality and offers a more stable environment for producers to make decisions regarding seasonal batches, contracts, and pricing negotiations, compared to a rapid surge in supply.
 
