This article from the International Cheese Federation''s blog discusses common challenges in producing blue cheese, particularly issues leading to patchy veining. It explains the critical role of oxygen for Penicillium roqueforti mold growth, the importance of correct piercing timing, and proper curd handling. The post highlights how the federation''s blue cheese production course addresses these troubleshooting techniques, covering culture selection, curd handling, salting, piercing windows, and aging room environmental control to help cheesemakers achieve consistent product quality.
 
