This article details a workshop by the International Cheese Federation focused on helping cheesemakers develop and maintain robust food safety plans and documentation to meet federal regulatory compliance. It emphasizes the importance of written plans, hazard analysis, preventive controls, and record-keeping, particularly for soft and semi-soft cheese production, to avoid inspection failures. The workshop is presented as routine maintenance for compliance paperwork, not a one-time solution.
 
